{
  "$schema": "../gen/schemas/desktop-schema.json",
  "identifier": "main",
  "description": "Main window. Grants only the app's own IPC commands. No core:* permission is granted: the UI calls nothing but invoke() of app commands, and Channel delivery (__TAURI_CHANNEL__ fetch) is not ACL-gated. No plugin permission is granted but one: dialog/opener/window-state/log/updater/notification are driven from Rust only, so their JS APIs stay unreachable from the webview. The exception is notification:allow-is-permission-granted, a read-only query the notification plugin's own init script sends on every page load (granted always on desktop); without it each load logs a denied invoke. notify, request_permission and every other notification command stay denied.",
